2026-10-21 PHP security patch

See 
   https://almalinux.org/blog/2026-10-21-php2shell-cve-2026-109618-cve-2026-109619/
   https://www.huntress.com/blog/php2shell-leaked-critical-php-vulnerabilities


Affects PHP 8.2.34, patches in 8.2.35 and 8.2.36 (?)

10/21 13:20 -- 8.2.35 still not available for almalinux 8

====Mitigation strategy============

Add to /etc/php.ini
   ; Mitigate PHP2Shell vulnerabilities by disabling upload progress tracking
   session.upload_progress.enabled = Off
   session.upload_progress.cleanup = Off
   memory_limit = -1
   upload_max_filesize = 30M

Add to /etc/php-fpm.d/www.conf
   php_admin_value[memory_limit] = -1

Run
   systemctl restart php-fpm
   systemctl restart httpd

Check:
   php -r "var_dump(ini_get('session.upload_progress.enabled'));"

   should produce:
      string(0) ""

   Make sure we're not using mod_php:
      httpd -M | grep php

